title: Expelled from the Soviet Executive
subtitle: 14 June 1918.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: player_party != 'lsr' and (dix >= 34 and bol_regime = 1)
priority: 40
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.expelled_check = (Q.ally_bol >= 2 || (Q.soviet_democracy >= 65 && Q.spring_honoured)) ? 0 : 1;
if (Q.expelled_check) {
    if (Q.legality > 1) { Q.legality = 1; }
    Q.expelled = 1;
    RO.add(Q, {repression: 4, soviet_democracy: -4});
}
!}
go-to: expel_yes if expelled_check = 1; expel_no if expelled_check = 0

@expel_yes

= Expelled

On 14 June the Central Executive Committee, on a motion by Sverdlov, expelled the Mensheviks (the "Menshevik-Defencists") from its membership, on the ground that they were linked to the counter-revolutionary forces on the Volga. The decision is later extended to the SRs, and, in July, to the soviets as a whole.

Our press has been closed in a dozen cities and our deputies expelled from the soviets of a dozen more. The party is not banned. It is not legal either.

- @protest: Protest, and stay within the law.
- @underground: Go underground.
- @pledge: Pledge non-violence in return for readmission.

@protest
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: -3});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -2);
!}

We protested in the press, and went on holding meetings in those factories where they would let us.

@underground
on-arrival: {!
Q.underground = 1;
Q.members -= 18 * Q.mem_scale;
for (var g of RO.BOOST_GROUPS) { Q['boost_' + g] = (Q['boost_' + g] || 0) * 0.5; }
RO.add(Q, {repression: -3});
Q.resources += 1;
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 4);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 4);
!}

The party printing presses are in cellars and its meetings in apartments. We are safe from the Cheka's attention, and invisible to everybody else.

@pledge
choose-if: armed_struggle = 0
unavailable-subtitle: We have been in touch with Komuch, and nobody would believe the pledge.
on-arrival: {!
Q.readmission_hope = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 4, repression: -1});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 10);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 4);
!}

The Central Committee has pledged that the party will never resort to armed struggle against the Soviet government, and asked to be readmitted. The Bolsheviks have said that they will consider it. [+ Rlbl +] are aghast.

@expel_no

= The Expulsion Is Averted

On 14 June the Central Executive Committee considered a motion to expel the Mensheviks. It was opposed by the Left SRs, by the moderate Bolsheviks, and by the evidence of the spring elections, which showed that the Mensheviks speak for a large part of the workers. The motion was withdrawn.

We remain a legal party in the soviets, with all our rights, and the knowledge that nobody has any rights for long.
